  </data>
  <data name="Gt_L324.Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>After my friend joins, what does he do in the game?</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Gt_L326.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Friend's side</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Gt_L335.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>•</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Gt_L350.Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Friend can't connect? Check these in order</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Gt_L352.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>1. Your friend must first run the one-click join script (or paste the invite code); the address only works in his game after he joins.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Gt_L357.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>2. Your game must be up (room created or server started) and listening on the port above (this page checks automatically).</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Gt_L362.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>3. Use “Network Check” to see whether you're on a relay — relay still works, but with higher latency.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Gt_L367.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>4. If it still fails, have your friend disable his security suite's network protection temporarily — some suites block Tailscale.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Gt_InviteBox.PlaceholderText" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>TBG1:… or 100.101.102.103:25565</value>
  </data>
